{"schema":1,"id":"just-bash","title":"Why must you keep the returned shell?","lang":"en","sources":["https://github.com/elixir-ai-tools/just_bash","https://github.com/ivarvong/lantern/blob/2c7bad5/scenes/just-bash.ts"],"settings":[],"answer":"exec returns a new shell holding the write and leaves the shell you passed in unchanged","checks":[{"question":"From the empty shell, a caller runs echo hi > a.txt and keeps the returned shell. Then it runs echo bye > b.txt on the empty shell again and keeps that result too. Which files does the second result hold, and where is a.txt?","answer":"The second result holds b.txt and nothing else. a.txt is in the first result, because the second command started from the empty shell, which never received the first write."},{"question":"Run echo hello | tr a-z A-Z with no redirect. What does exec print, and does the returned shell gain a file?","answer":"It prints \"HELLO\\n\", and the returned shell holds no files. Without a redirect the text stays on standard output, so there is no write for the returned shell to carry."},{"question":"To check whether shout.txt exists, a caller runs ls on the returned shell. What happens, and what does that tell it about the file?","answer":"exec throws “Unknown model command: ls”, because this model has branches only for echo, tr and cat. The error says nothing about shout.txt; cat on the returned shell would print its contents."}],"scenarios":[{"values":{},"name":"","duration":148.967,"paper":"#17362f","invariants":["s0 stays the empty shell"],"machines":[{"events":["RUN_PIPELINE","CAT_NEWEST","CAT_S0","LS"],"start":{"shells":[{"fs":{},"steps":0}],"cats":[null]},"states":6,"step":"lesson"}],"steps":[{"step":"reader-pipeline","title":"The command ran, yet cat finds nothing in shout.txt","line":"Predict: where did HELLO go?","caption":"Run echo hello | tr a-z A-Z > shout.txt in a small in-memory shell. echo produces hello and a newline, tr uppercases it, and the redirect stores HELLO in shout.txt instead of printing it. Then run cat shout.txt on the shell you started with: it prints nothing, and nothing reported an error. This model hands strings from command to command; it does not run an operating-system shell.","start":0,"end":25.133,"hold":0.567,"state":{"file":"HELLO\n","stdout":"","startingCat":""},"changed":{"file":{"after":"HELLO\n"},"stdout":{"after":""},"startingCat":{"after":""}},"picture":"Echo hello. tr → HELLO. shout.txt. hello. HELLO. cat shout.txt on the starting shell:. prints nothing.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│                              hello                         HELLO\n│\n│     ┌──────────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────────┐        ┌─────────────────────┐\n│     │                      │       │                     │        │                     │\n│     │     echo hello       ────────▶     tr → HELLO      ─────────▶      shout.txt      │\n│     └──────────────────────┘       └─────────────────────┘        └─────────────────────┘\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│                             cat shout.txt on the starting shell:\n│\n│\n│                                        prints nothing\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│"},{"step":"reader-values","title":"Answer: the file is in the shell exec returned","line":"Same command, two shell values: only the returned one holds shout.txt.","caption":"In this model, exec returns a new shell holding the write and leaves the shell you passed in unchanged. cat prints HELLO with the returned shell and prints nothing with the original, which still has no files. A caller that drops the return value has thrown away the shell that holds the write, although the command ran.","start":25.133,"end":46.533,"hold":25.867,"state":{"old":"","next":"HELLO\n","file":"HELLO\n"},"changed":{"stdout":{"before":""},"startingCat":{"before":""},"old":{"after":""},"next":{"after":"HELLO\n"}},"picture":"Shell. shout.txt. cat prints. original. missing. nothing. returned. HELLO. HELLO.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│            Shell                          shout.txt                    cat prints\n│          ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│            original                       missing                      nothing\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│             returned                      HELLO                         HELLO\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│"},{"step":"command","title":"A command line and the empty shell it runs on","line":"Two commands, a pipe and a redirect; the shell starts with no files.","caption":"This executable model follows the JustBash example: a pipeline transforms strings and a redirect writes an in-memory filesystem. The shell starts as a plain value with no files.","start":46.533,"end":57.033,"hold":49.033,"state":{"old":"","next":"HELLO\n","file":"HELLO\n"},"changed":{},"picture":"Code, 3 lines; 10 labels. Focused: 1: shell = { fs: {}, steps: 0 }.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│                echo hello        |        tr a-z A-Z         >       shout.txt\n│           ▌                     ▌    ▌                      ▌   ▌\n│                  command       pipe         command      redirect      file\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│                            ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                            │▌shell = { fs: {}, steps: 0 }        │\n│                            │▌                                    │\n│                            │ exec(shell, pipeline, redirect)     │\n│                            │   → { shell, stdout }               │\n│                            └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n│\n│\n│"},{"step":"parse","title":"The command line parses into a tree","line":"Echo and tr sit under the pipeline; the redirect is not a command.","caption":"A script holds a pipeline of two commands, echo and tr; the redirect records where the final output goes. The tree becomes the arguments the executor receives.","start":57.033,"end":67.167,"hold":61.3,"state":{"old":"","next":"HELLO\n","file":"HELLO\n"},"changed":{},"picture":"Flowchart: 5 nodes, 4 links; Code, 4 lines. Note: “not a command” beside redirect to shout.txt; marked: echo hello; tr a-z A-Z; focused: 2: [[\"echo\", \"hello\"]; and 1 more. New in this step: Script; Script → Pipeline; Script → redirect to shout.txt; and 5 more.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  │                                                         │\n│  │                          ┌─────────┐                    │\n│  │                          │ ──────  │                    │\n│  │                 ┌────────│───┌─────│───────┐            │\n│  │                 │        └─────────┘       │            │  ┌────────────────────────────┐\n│  │                 │─           ││           ─│            │  │ exec(shell,                │\n│  │            ┌──────────┐──────└───┌───────────────────┐  │  ▌   [[\"echo\", \"hello\"],      │\n│  │            │ ──────── │          │ ────────────────  │  │  ▌                            │\n│  │          ┌─└──────────┘─┐        └───────────────────┘  │  ▌    [\"tr\", \"a-z\", \"A-Z\"]],  │\n│  │          │     │  │     │            not a command      │  │   \"shout.txt\")             │\n│  │   ┌────────────┐  ┌────────────┐                        │  └────────────────────────────┘\n│  │   │  ──────────│  │──────────  │                        │\n│  │   │            │  │    ── ──   │                        │\n│  │   └────────────┘  └────────────┘                        │\n│  │                                                         │\n│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n│\n│\n│"},{"step":"reduce","title":"A pipeline is a reduce over strings","line":"Echo sets stdout to \"hello\\n\"; tr turns it into \"HELLO\\n\".","caption":"Start with empty text. Echo replaces it with hello and a newline, and tr uppercases it. The note under each builtin is stdout after it runs: one string handed to the next, with no kernel pipe between them.","start":67.167,"end":81.433,"hold":75.4,"state":{"oldShell":{"fs":{},"steps":0},"newShell":{"fs":{"shout.txt":"HELLO\n"},"steps":2},"stdout":"","walks":[{"step":"reduce","from":"Input","to":"Echo","edge":"edge:Input->Echo#0"},{"step":"reduce","from":"Echo","to":"Tr","edge":"edge:Echo->Tr#0"},{"step":"reduce","from":"Tr","to":"Output","edge":"edge:Tr->Output#0"}]},"changed":{"old":{"before":""},"next":{"before":"HELLO\n"},"file":{"before":"HELLO\n"},"oldShell":{"after":{"fs":{},"steps":0}},"newShell":{"after":{"fs":{"shout.txt":"HELLO\n"},"steps":2}},"stdout":{"after":""},"walks":{"after":[{"step":"reduce","from":"Input","to":"Echo","edge":"edge:Input->Echo#0"},{"step":"reduce","from":"Echo","to":"Tr","edge":"edge:Echo->Tr#0"},{"step":"reduce","from":"Tr","to":"Output","edge":"edge:Tr->Output#0"}]}},"picture":"Flowchart: 4 nodes, 3 links; Code, 4 lines. Travelled: empty stdin → echo hello; echo hello → tr a-z A-Z; tr a-z A-Z → stdout; note: “\"hello\\n\"” beside echo hello; and 2 more. New in this step: empty stdin; stdout; Code, 4 lines.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│  ▌\n│  ▌\n│  ▌    ┌─────────────────┐    ┌────────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐     ┌────────────┐\n│  ▌    │                 │    │                │     │              │     │            │\n│  ▌    │   ───────────  ─│────│─  ───────────  │─────│  ──────────  │─────│  ────────  │\n│  ▌    └─────────────────┘    └────────────────┘     │              │     └────────────┘\n│  ▌                                ────────          └──────────────┘\n│  ▌                                \"hello\\n\"            \"HELLO\\n\"\n│  ▌\n│\n│\n│\n│                          ┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                          │                                         │\n│                          │ stdout = \"\"                             │\n│                          │ for each [name, ...args] in stages:     │\n│                          │   echo: stdout = args + \"\\n\"            │\n│                          ▌                                         │\n│                          ▌   tr:   stdout = upper(stdout)          │\n│                          └─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n│\n│"},{"step":"redirect","title":"The redirect writes into a copy, and exec returns the copy","line":"The returned shell holds shout.txt; the original still has no files.","caption":"The redirect stores HELLO in shout.txt and empties stdout, but the file does not go into the shell the caller passed in. exec copies that shell’s files into a new shell value, adds shout.txt there and returns it, so the original shell on the left still has no files and its step count is still 0.","start":81.433,"end":102.433,"hold":85.5,"state":{"oldShell":{"fs":{},"steps":0},"newShell":{"fs":{"shout.txt":"HELLO\n"},"steps":2},"stdout":"","walks":[{"step":"reduce","from":"Input","to":"Echo","edge":"edge:Input->Echo#0"},{"step":"reduce","from":"Echo","to":"Tr","edge":"edge:Echo->Tr#0"},{"step":"reduce","from":"Tr","to":"Output","edge":"edge:Tr->Output#0"}]},"changed":{},"picture":"Flowchart: 4 nodes, 3 links; “Original shell”, 2 labelled values; “Returned shell”, 4 labelled values. Note: “\"HELLO\\n\"” beside shout.txt; marked: files: none; shout.txt: \"HELLO\\n\". New in this step: tr a-z A-Z → shout.txt; shout.txt; “Original shell”, 2 labelled values; and 1 more.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│  ▌\n│  ▌\n│  ▌    ┌────────────────┐     ┌───────────────┐    ┌───────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐\n│  ▌    │                │     │               │    │               │    │              │\n│  ▌    │  ────────────  │─────│  ───────────  │────│─  ─────────   │────│─  ─────────  │\n│  ▌    └────────────────┘     └───────────────┘    │               │    └──────────────┘\n│  ▌                                                └───────────────┘       ─\"HELLO\\n\"\n│  ▌\n│  ▌\n│\n│        ┌──────────────────────────────┐               ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n│        │ Original shell               │               │Returned shell                │\n│        │▌                             │               │                              │\n│        │▌files                   none │               │files              shout.txt  │\n│        │▌                             │               ▌                              │\n│        │ steps run                  0 │               ▌shout.txt          \"HELLO\\n\"  │\n│        │                              │               ▌                              │\n│        └──────────────────────────────┘               │steps run                  2  │\n│                                                       │stdout                    \"\"  │\n│                                                       │                              │\n│                                                       └──────────────────────────────┘\n│"},{"step":"lookup","title":"The model runs echo, tr and cat and refuses ls","line":"A name with no branch falls to the last line and throws.","caption":"Exec dispatches on the command name: echo, tr and cat each have a branch, and any other name, such as ls, falls through to the last line and throws “Unknown model command”.","start":102.433,"end":114.433,"hold":109.533,"state":{"oldShell":{"fs":{},"steps":0},"newShell":{"fs":{"shout.txt":"HELLO\n"},"steps":2},"stdout":"","walks":[{"step":"reduce","from":"Input","to":"Echo","edge":"edge:Input->Echo#0"},{"step":"reduce","from":"Echo","to":"Tr","edge":"edge:Echo->Tr#0"},{"step":"reduce","from":"Tr","to":"Output","edge":"edge:Tr->Output#0"},{"step":"lookup","from":"Name","to":"Builtin","edge":"edge:Name->Builtin#0"},{"step":"lookup","from":"Builtin","to":"Run","edge":"edge:Builtin->Run#0"},{"step":"lookup","from":"Builtin","to":"Error","edge":"edge:Builtin->Error#0"}]},"changed":{"walks":{"before":[{"step":"reduce","from":"Input","to":"Echo","edge":"edge:Input->Echo#0"},{"step":"reduce","from":"Echo","to":"Tr","edge":"edge:Echo->Tr#0"},{"step":"reduce","from":"Tr","to":"Output","edge":"edge:Tr->Output#0"}],"after":[{"step":"reduce","from":"Input","to":"Echo","edge":"edge:Input->Echo#0"},{"step":"reduce","from":"Echo","to":"Tr","edge":"edge:Echo->Tr#0"},{"step":"reduce","from":"Tr","to":"Output","edge":"edge:Tr->Output#0"},{"step":"lookup","from":"Name","to":"Builtin","edge":"edge:Name->Builtin#0"},{"step":"lookup","from":"Builtin","to":"Run","edge":"edge:Builtin->Run#0"},{"step":"lookup","from":"Builtin","to":"Error","edge":"edge:Builtin->Error#0"}]}},"picture":"Flowchart: 4 nodes, 3 links; Code, 4 lines. Note: “echo · tr · cat” beside found: run on values; “ls” beside missing: refuse; travelled: command name → look up the builtin; look up the builtin → found: run on values; and 2 more.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│           ▌                                                    ───────────\n│           ▌                                                  echo · tr · cat\n│           ▌                                               ┌───────────────────┐\n│           ▌                                         ┌─────│ ───────────────── │\n│           ▌   ┌───────────────┐    ┌─────────────────┐    └───────────────────┘\n│           ▌   │  ──────────── │────│ ────────────── ┌│────┌───────────────────┐\n│           ▌   └───────────────┘    └─────────────────┘   ─│   ─────────────   │\n│           ▌                                         └─────│                   │\n│           ▌                                               └───────────────────┘\n│           ▌                                                        ls\n│           ▌\n│\n│\n│                       ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                       │                                               │\n│                       │ if (name === \"echo\") …                        │\n│                       │ else if (name === \"tr\") …                     │\n│                       │ else if (name === \"cat\") …                    │\n│                       ▌                                               │\n│                       ▌ else throw Error(\"Unknown model command\")     │\n│                       └───────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n│\n│"},{"step":"cat","title":"cat reads the returned shell","line":"The returned shell has shout.txt, so cat prints HELLO.","caption":"Cat receives the returned shell, finds shout.txt and prints HELLO. The write is visible because the caller passed exec’s returned shell to this call; the original would print nothing.","start":114.433,"end":125.333,"hold":117.067,"state":{"oldShell":{"fs":{},"steps":0},"newShell":{"fs":{"shout.txt":"HELLO\n"},"steps":2},"stdout":"","walks":[{"step":"reduce","from":"Input","to":"Echo","edge":"edge:Input->Echo#0"},{"step":"reduce","from":"Echo","to":"Tr","edge":"edge:Echo->Tr#0"},{"step":"reduce","from":"Tr","to":"Output","edge":"edge:Tr->Output#0"},{"step":"lookup","from":"Name","to":"Builtin","edge":"edge:Name->Builtin#0"},{"step":"lookup","from":"Builtin","to":"Run","edge":"edge:Builtin->Run#0"},{"step":"lookup","from":"Builtin","to":"Error","edge":"edge:Builtin->Error#0"}],"cat":"HELLO\n"},"changed":{"cat":{"after":"HELLO\n"}},"picture":"Code, 1 line; “Original shell”, 3 labelled values; “Returned shell”, 3 labelled values. Marked: cat stdout: \"HELLO\\n\".","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│                  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                  │ exec(returned, [[\"cat\", \"shout.txt\"]])                  │\n│                  │                                                         │\n│                  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│            ┌───────────────────────┐                   ┌───────────────────────────┐\n│            │Original shell         │                   │ Returned shell            │\n│            │                       │                   │                           │\n│            │files            none  │                   │ files          shout.txt  │\n│            │                       │                   │                           │\n│            │shout.txt     missing  │                   │ shout.txt      \"HELLO\\n\"  │\n│            │                       │                   ▌                           │\n│            │cat stdout         \"\"  │                   ▌ cat stdout     \"HELLO\\n\"  │\n│            └───────────────────────┘                   └───────────────────────────┘\n│\n│\n│\n│"},{"step":"lesson","title":"Keep the returned shell: the caller holds both and can cat either","line":"On s1 cat prints HELLO, on s0 it prints nothing; s0.fs is still {}.","caption":"Call the starting shell s0 and the shell exec returned s1. exec gives back the next shell and leaves its input alone, so the caller holds both at once: cat on s1 prints HELLO and cat on s0 prints nothing. Code that passes s1 to the next command sees the file; code that keeps using s0 has lost it, although the command ran.","start":125.333,"end":148.967,"hold":132.533,"state":{"shells":[{"fs":{},"steps":0},{"fs":{"shout.txt":"HELLO\n"},"steps":2}],"cats":["","HELLO\n"],"walks":[{"step":"reduce","from":"Input","to":"Echo","edge":"edge:Input->Echo#0"},{"step":"reduce","from":"Echo","to":"Tr","edge":"edge:Echo->Tr#0"},{"step":"reduce","from":"Tr","to":"Output","edge":"edge:Tr->Output#0"},{"step":"lookup","from":"Name","to":"Builtin","edge":"edge:Name->Builtin#0"},{"step":"lookup","from":"Builtin","to":"Run","edge":"edge:Builtin->Run#0"},{"step":"lookup","from":"Builtin","to":"Error","edge":"edge:Builtin->Error#0"}]},"changed":{"oldShell":{"before":{"fs":{},"steps":0}},"newShell":{"before":{"fs":{"shout.txt":"HELLO\n"},"steps":2}},"stdout":{"before":""},"cat":{"before":"HELLO\n"},"shells":{"after":[{"fs":{},"steps":0},{"fs":{"shout.txt":"HELLO\n"},"steps":2}]},"cats":{"after":["","HELLO\n"]}},"picture":"S0, the original shell, holds files: none. s1, the returned shell, which the caller keeps, holds files: shout.txt. An arrow from s0 to s1: echo, tr, redirect. cat shout.txt on s0 prints nothing. cat shout.txt on s1 prints HELLO.; Code, 4 lines. Focused: 2: exec(s1, [[\"cat\", \"shout.txt\"]]).stdout // \"HELLO\\n\".","events":["RUN_PIPELINE","CAT_NEWEST","CAT_S0"],"drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│         ┌─────────────────────┐                       ┌────────────────────┐\n│         │ s0: original shell  │  echo, tr, redirect   │ s1: returned shell │\n│         │     files: none     ───────────────────────▶│  files: shout.txt  │\n│         └─────────────────────┘                       └────────────────────┘\n│                    │                                             │\n│                    │cat shout.txt                                │cat shout.txt\n│                    │                                             │\n│           ┌────────▼────────┐                           ┌────────▼────────┐\n│           │ prints nothing  │                           │  prints HELLO   │\n│           └─────────────────┘                           └─────────────────┘\n│\n│\n│                ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                │                                                             │\n│                ▌ s1 = exec(s0, pipeline, \"shout.txt\").shell                  │\n│                ▌ exec(s1, [[\"cat\", \"shout.txt\"]]).stdout   // \"HELLO\\n\"      │\n│                ▌ exec(s0, [[\"cat\", \"shout.txt\"]]).stdout   // \"\"             │\n│                │                                                             │\n│                │ s0.fs                               // {}                   │\n│                └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n│\n│\nevent · event · event"}]}]}